Review brief:
Prepare a focused review of when batch adsorption results do and do not predict column, pilot, or full-scale PFAS treatment performance.

Required components:
[{"requirement":"Compare the information provided by equilibrium capacity, kinetics, fixed-bed breakthrough, bed volumes treated, and media lifetime."},{"requirement":"Assess how flow, contact time, influent variability, competing constituents, and PFAS mixtures affect translation across scales."},{"requirement":"Identify the minimum evidence needed to support a defensible service-life or scale-up claim."}]

Task boundaries:
{"constraints":[{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if batch capacity or short kinetic performance is presented as direct evidence of column breakthrough or field lifetime."},{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if scale-up claims omit flow, contact time, influent variability, competing constituents, PFAS mixture, or breakthrough definition."}],"task_boundaries":"Translation of adsorption evidence across batch, column, pilot, and full-scale treatment; equilibrium capacity is not equivalent to service life."}

Held-out anchor identifiers:
{"all_blocked_dois":["10.1016/j.envpol.2023.121138"],"all_blocked_titles":["a review of pfas adsorption from aqueous solutions current approaches engineering applications challenges and opportunities"],"all_blocked_urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2023.121138"],"anchor_id":"AR-LEI-2023","corpus_source":"2023 - Lei - A review of PFAS adsorption from aqueous solutions - Current approaches, engineering applications, challenges, and opportunities.pdf","doi":"10.1016/j.envpol.2023.121138","title":"A review of PFAS adsorption from aqueous solutions: Current approaches, engineering applications, challenges, and opportunities","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envpol.2023.121138"}

